      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "{\u0022risks\u0022:[{\u0022risk\u0022:\u0022that supply stays short of demand, so orders cannot be turned into revenue as fast as they arrive\u0022,\u0022riskDocument\u0022:3,\u0022confirm\u0022:{\u0022event\u0022:\u0022management reports that component shortages have delayed shipments and held back revenue conversion in a coming quarter\u0022,\u0022kind\u0022:\u0022supply\u0022},\u0022why\u0022:\u0022management said demand is far exceeding its ability to supply, that the supply environment is less flexible than a year ago, and that supply will govern near-term revenue for the next several quarters\u0022,\u0022whyDocument\u0022:3},{\u0022risk\u0022:\u0022that profitability slips back once the one-time tariff benefit that lifted this year\u0027s results does not repeat\u0022,\u0022riskDocument\u0022:3,\u0022confirm\u0022:{\u0022fact\u0022:\u0022latest quarter net margin\u0022},\u0022direction\u0022:\u0022falls below\u0022,\u0022level\u0022:\u002221.51%\u0022,\u0022why\u0022:\u0022the chief financial officer said one-time tariff impacts artificially pulled up profitability this year and will not repeat, so a lower net margin would show that boost fading\u0022,\u0022whyDocument\u0022:3},{\u0022risk\u0022:\u0022that the valuation multiple compresses after the strong run in the shares\u0022,\u0022riskDocument\u0022:3,\u0022confirm\u0022:{\u0022fact\u0022:\u0022forward price to earnings\u0022},\u0022direction\u0022:\u0022falls below\u0022,\u0022level\u0022:\u002220.66\u0022,\u0022why\u0022:\u0022a fall in the forward multiple would show investors paying less for expected earnings, which fits the view that the valuation leaves little room for error\u0022,\u0022whyDocument\u0022:3},{\u0022risk\u0022:\u0022that AI infrastructure spending slows, since recent growth leans on data centre demand\u0022,\u0022riskDocument\u0022:2,\u0022confirm\u0022:{\u0022event\u0022:\u0022major hyperscale customers cut or delay AI data centre capital spending, and wireline orders fall\u0022,\u0022kind\u0022:\u0022other\u0022},\u0022why\u0022:\u0022the record results were driven by AI infrastructure demand, with wireline revenue passing wireless revenue for the first time, so growth depends on continued heavy capital spending by hyperscalers\u0022,\u0022whyDocument\u0022:2},{\u0022risk\u0022:\u0022that export control rules or tariff and trade policy hurt results\u0022,\u0022riskDocument\u0022:1,\u0022confirm\u0022:{\u0022event\u0022:\u0022new export control restrictions or tariffs are imposed that block sales or raise costs for the company\u0027s products\u0022,\u0022kind\u0022:\u0022regulatory\u0022},\u0022why\u0022:\u0022the company lists export control regulations and compliance, and tariff and trade policy impacts, among the uncertainties that could make results differ materially from expectations\u0022,\u0022whyDocument\u0022:1},{\u0022risk\u0022:\u0022that the Spirent integration delivers less than the planned cost savings\u0022,\u0022riskDocument\u0022:3,\u0022confirm\u0022:{\u0022event\u0022:\u0022management lowers its expectation for realised cost synergies from the recent acquisitions or reports new integration problems\u0022,\u0022kind\u0022:\u0022acquisition\u0022},\u0022why\u0022:\u0022management expects only 80% to 90% of the $100 million synergy target to be realised on a run rate basis by year end, so any cut to that range would show the savings falling short\u0022,\u0022whyDocument\u0022:3}]}"
